---
import RedesignLayout from '../../layouts/RedesignLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/band/PageHero.astro';
import RdFeature from '../../components/redesign/RdFeature.astro';
import ScriptBand from '../../components/redesign/ScriptBand.astro';
import LeafHeading from '../../components/redesign/LeafHeading.astro';
import RdCta from '../../components/redesign/RdCta.astro';
import VideoEmbed from '../../components/global/VideoEmbed.astro';

// The fruit of the first 90 national leaders (verbatim from the live story,
// see the 2004 entry below). `pre` + `num` + `post` reproduces each line
// exactly; `num` is only pulled out for visual emphasis.
const fruit = [
  { pre: 'Distributed ', num: '80,000+', post: ' Bibles' },
  { pre: 'Trained ', num: '7,000+', post: ' pastors' },
  { pre: 'Graduated ', num: '500+', post: ' leaders from a Bible college' },
  { pre: 'Reached ', num: '50,000+', post: ' through trauma counseling' },
  { pre: 'Held crusades with ', num: '1 million+', post: ' attending' },
  { pre: 'Conducted mobile medical clinics for ', num: '8,000+', post: ' patients' },
  { pre: 'Built a school with ', num: '400', post: ' attending' },
  { pre: '', num: '', post: 'Built the first Christian radio station' },
  { pre: '', num: '', post: 'Trained government leaders' },
];
---
<RedesignLayout
  title="Our Story"
  description="How Favor International started, where the founding conviction came from, and how the work grew across East Africa."
>
  <PageHero
    label="Our story"
    title="The conviction Favor was born from."
    promise="How one woman's prayer grew into an indigenous missions movement across East and Central Africa."
    image="/images/story-historic-prayer.jpg"
    imageAlt="A national prayer gathering in northern Uganda"
  />

  <RdFeature
    image="/images/field-2026/carole-1.webp"
    imageAlt="The original Favor House in northern Uganda"
    eyebrow="2002 to 2004"
    heading="The beginning."
    side="left"
  >
    <p>Carole Ward moved to Uganda in 2002 during a 20-year horrific war, serving and training African leaders from all backgrounds to pray. Together they saw the war end, and she began equipping them to reach their own people with the power of the Gospel.</p>
    <p>After six months of prayer, Ugandans came to her with desperate visions for reaching their own people with Bibles, discipleship, education, and evangelism. In 2004, Carole formed Favour of God Ministries and began training indigenous missionaries to run that vision.</p>
  </RdFeature>

  <ScriptBand
    image="/images/field-2026/carole-4.webp"
    imageAlt="Carole Ward in prayer in the field"
    label="The founding prayer"
    phrase="Lord, send me where no one wants to go, to do what no one wants to do."
    cite="Carole Ward, Founder"
    objectPosition="center 30%"
  />

  <section class="band band--cream">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <LeafHeading label="The story, year by year" title="How the work grew." leaves={false} />

      <div class="tl">
        <div class="tl-item">
          <span class="tl-year">2004</span>
          <div class="tl-content rd-prose">
            <div class="tl-photo" style="background-image:url('/images/field-2026/carole-2.webp')" role="img" aria-label="The original House of Prayer in Gulu"></div>
            <p>In time, after much intercessory prayer, many came to join Carole in the ministry of evangelism, Bible teaching, and caring for the orphans. When the government required registration to continue the work in this dangerous area, Carole formed the ministry in 2004, with two Ugandans. Though the needs were enormous, God told her, &ldquo;Build My house, and I&rsquo;ll build yours!&rdquo; (1 Chronicles 17:10 &amp; 25).</p>
            <p>Soon after, Favor opened a simple community called the House of Prayer in Gulu, the regional capital in the center of the war. It became a center for a missionary movement that was in part instrumental to end the war through the power of the Gospel.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tl-item">
          <span class="tl-year">2005</span>
          <div class="tl-content rd-prose">
            <div class="tl-photo" style="background-image:url('/images/field-2026/prayer-2.webp')" role="img" aria-label="The National Prayer Gathering in Gulu, 2005"></div>
            <p>A real turning point in our story was the National Prayer Gathering in Gulu. The Lord prompted us to organize a gathering in the War Memorial Stadium to unify the tribes, leaders, churches, and regions in Uganda in repentant prayer for the ending of the war. We planned a 77 hour prayer meeting, 11 hours a day for 7 days in December 2005. Radio stations were contacted to spread the news and word spread like wildfire. The day finally approached and over 1,000 people, including political leaders, gathered inside this humble stadium to join in intense, radical, united prayer.</p>
            <p>As a result, the war stopped and many significant stories of radical transformation followed. Pastors reported that they sensed heaven opening in a new way. Government officials called and testified of a strong sense that the spiritual climate over the area had changed. Miracles were occurring in local churches. It even led to inaugurating the month of January as the month of prayer.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tl-item">
          <span class="tl-year">2007 to 2014</span>
          <div class="tl-content rd-prose">
            <div class="tl-photo" style="background-image:url('/images/field-2026/education-1.webp')" role="img" aria-label="Graduates celebrating in DR Congo"></div>
            <p>In 2007, the Lord led Carole to begin extending the work into Sudan before liberation. National prayer gatherings were mobilized in Juba, the capital of South Sudan, in 2015 and again in 2019, to see enough peace for the Gospel to extend to the farthest regions of the nation and into the most remote tribes and villages. In 2014, FAMI was birthed as a sister organization to FOGM in Northern Uganda, with the same vision, prayer foundation, and indigenous leadership development in each country.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tl-item">
          <span class="tl-year">2015 to now</span>
          <div class="tl-content rd-prose">
            <div class="tl-photo" style="background-image:url('/images/field/prayer-gathering-chad.webp')" role="img" aria-label="A national prayer gathering in Chad"></div>
            <p>We began to focus more direct efforts to South Sudan in 2007 by sending missionaries and Portable Bible School (PBS) programs. We organized a legal presence in the nation through trusted Portable Bible School graduates and purchased our first office space in Juba in 2015. That same year we hosted a national prayer meeting in Juba, the capital of South Sudan, just as we did in Uganda, to bring God&rsquo;s repentance, revival, and restoration.</p>
            <p>In the years since, we have continued establishing Houses of Prayer in strategic locations across Uganda and South Sudan. In the early part of 2024, we also established a House of Prayer in N&rsquo;Djamena, the capital city of Chad.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band rd-fruit-band">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="label label--inverse rd-fruit-band__eyebrow">The fruit</p>
      <p class="rd-fruit-band__lead">The ministry quickly grew to 90 national leaders in a few years. Those 90 leaders:</p>
      <ul class="rd-fruit-grid">
        {fruit.map((f) => (
          <li class={f.num ? 'rd-fruit-stat' : 'rd-fruit-stat rd-fruit-stat--text'}>
            {f.num && <span class="rd-fruit-stat__num">{f.num}</span>}
            <span class="rd-fruit-stat__cap">{f.num ? `${f.pre.trim()} ${f.post.trim()}` : f.post}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ScriptBand
    image="/images/hero-pastor-preaching.jpg"
    imageAlt="An indigenous pastor preaching to a gathered crowd under an acacia tree"
    label="The vision"
    phrase="Every tribe and language reaching their own people, and beyond, with the power of God's Word."
    font="serif"
    objectPosition="center 40%"
  />

  <section class="band band--white">
    <div class="container container--narrow founder-film">
      <LeafHeading label="In her own words" title="Hear the story from Carole." />
      <VideoEmbed id="g2fB1RwyHNM" title="The Carole Ward Story" />
      <p class="founder-film__link"><a href="/about/our-story/founder/" class="story-link">Read the full founder's story &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <RdFeature
    image="/images/field-2026/missionaries-5.webp"
    imageAlt="Favor field and office leaders together"
    eyebrow="Today"
    heading="Indigenous-led, across East Africa."
    side="right"
    background="cream"
  >
    <p>Favor International serves and trains indigenous leaders across East Africa. Each field team is led by African nationals. The U.S. team raises support, stewards funds, and provides accountability so the field can do the work it was called to.</p>
  </RdFeature>

  <RdCta
    heading="Be part of the next chapter."
    body="Favor Partners keep this story going. Monthly partnership, any tier, makes the field work possible."
    ctaLabel="Become a Favor Partner"
    ctaHref="/give/partner-monthly/"
    background="cream"
    image="/images/field/country-uganda.webp"
    imageAlt="A vision-trip team with Karamojong villagers in the savanna"
  />
</RedesignLayout>

<style>
  /* Vertical timeline, with real air between chapters */
  .tl { position: relative; }
  .tl-item { position: relative; padding-left: 72px; padding-bottom: clamp(64px, 8vw, 112px); }
  .tl-item:last-child { padding-bottom: 0; }
  .tl-item::after { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 11px; top: 6px; bottom: 0; width: 2px; background: var(--color-sage-light); }
  .tl-item:last-child::after { background: linear-gradient(var(--color-sage-light), transparent); }
  .tl-item::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 4px; top: 4px; width: 16px; height: 16px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--color-gold); box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px var(--color-cream); z-index: 1; }
  .tl-year { display: block; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: var(--rd-fs-title); color: var(--color-gold-deep); line-height: 1; margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .tl-photo { aspect-ratio: 16 / 8; background-size: cover; background-position: center 35%; border-radius: var(--rd-radius); box-shadow: var(--rd-shadow); margin: 0 0 var(--space-8); }
  .tl-content p { margin: 0 0 var(--space-5); }

  /* The fruit of the 90 leaders: its own deep-green proof band, big gold
     numbers, generous grid (verbatim copy via the data split). */
  .rd-fruit-band { background: var(--color-green-deep); color: var(--color-white); text-align: center; }
  .rd-fruit-band__eyebrow { display: block; }
  .rd-fruit-band__lead {
    max-width: 44ch; margin: var(--space-2) auto 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--rd-fs-sub); line-height: 1.35; color: var(--color-white);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .rd-fruit-grid {
    list-style: none; padding: 0;
    margin: clamp(48px, 6vw, 80px) auto 0; max-width: 1000px;
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(36px, 4vw, 56px) var(--space-8);
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .rd-fruit-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
  @media (max-width: 440px) { .rd-fruit-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .rd-fruit-stat { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); align-items: center; }
  .rd-fruit-stat__num {
    font-family: var(--font-sans); font-weight: 800;
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 5vw, 3.6rem); line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-gold);
  }
  .rd-fruit-stat__cap { font-size: var(--rd-fs-small); letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-white) 80%, transparent); line-height: 1.4; }
  .rd-fruit-stat--text { justify-content: center; }
  .rd-fruit-stat--text .rd-fruit-stat__cap { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--rd-fs-body); font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-gold-light); }

  .founder-film { text-align: center; }
  .founder-film :global(.video-embed) { max-width: 820px; margin-inline: auto; }
  .founder-film__link { margin-top: var(--space-8); }
  .story-link { color: var(--color-green); font-weight: 700; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-gold); }
</style>
